course: dictionary
lesson: 1481
title: Catkins in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Catkin is a new word, but the words around it leave clues. Read this: «Willow catkins are flowers, soft like a cat's paw.» Flowers and soft tell you the catkin is a kind of flower that feels soft.
explain: The dictionary meaning is a long, thin, soft cluster of tiny flowers that hangs from a tree. Swap it into the sentence: "Willow long, thin, soft clusters of tiny flowers are early food for bees." It still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Catkins grow on trees such as willow, hazel and birch. In spring, children find them in science and nature lessons. The wind carries their pollen, so the flowers help the trees spread it.
explain: The name pussy willow is a clue too. «Which is why people call them pussy willow», because the catkins are soft and furry, like a cat's paw. When you meet a word you do not know, look at the words around it first.
fact: A catkin is a long, thin, soft hanging cluster of tiny flowers.
fact: Catkins grow on trees such as willow, hazel and birch.
fact: «Pussy willow» is a name for willow catkins, because they look soft and furry like a cat's paw.
fact: Catkins spread pollen on the wind.
fact: Catkins are early food for bees.
exercise: «Willow catkins are flowers, soft like a cat's paw.» What is a catkin? | *A long, thin, soft hanging cluster of tiny flowers | A hard brown seed inside a shell | A small green leaf that falls in autumn | A type of cat's paw
exercise: Which trees have catkins in the lessons? | Palm, cedar and maple | Rose, lily and tulip | Oak, pine and holly | *Willow, hazel and birch
exercise: Why do people call them pussy willow? | Because cats climb willow trees | Because the flowers are bright orange | Because willows only grow near farms | *Because the catkins are soft and furry like a cat's paw
test: What do catkins spread on the wind? | Water | *Pollen | Seeds in shells | Leaves
test: Catkins are early food for which insects? | Ants | *Bees | Flies | Spiders
exam: Read: «Pussy willow catkins are soft and furry, and they are early food for bees.» What does early food mean here? | Food that grows underground | Food that is only for cats | Food that is burnt | *Food for bees that appears early in the year
